-	 * EXT_CSD again. LBA 1 holds the GPT header, which begins with the ASCII bytes
-	 * "EFI PART". If PIO delivers real content here, the all-zero EXT_CSD is specific
-	 * to that command; if this reads zeros as well, the data path itself is broken and
-	 * the next step is SDMA rather than more guessing. A static buffer keeps the
-	 * 512-byte payload off the stack.
+	 * boot-irq43/boot-irq56: prove the data path with a payload we can recognise
+	 * before trusting EXT_CSD again. LBA 1 holds the GPT header, which begins with
+	 * the ASCII bytes "EFI PART". The same block is read twice in this image, so the
